<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis XIV</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis XIV was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1643 to 1715, whose long reign marked the height of royal absolutism. Under his minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert">Colbert</a>, France expanded its colonies, navy and overseas trading companies, laying foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>. His invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in 1672 was a major military threat to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-xiv.jpg" alt="Louis XIV" width="296" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hyacinthe Rigaud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_XIV_of_France.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
